# Retail Performance Dashboard — Power BI



A multi-page Power BI dashboard analyzing retail Sales, Customer behaviour, and Product performance — built to support data-driven business decisions.

---

## Dashboard Preview

> Download the `.pbix` file and open in Power BI Desktop to explore the interactive report.

| Sales Overview | Customer Analysis | Product Performance |
|---|---|---|
| ![](Screenshots/sales_overview.png) | ![](Screenshots/customer_analysis.png) | ![](Screenshots/product_performance.png) |

---

## Key Business Questions

- Which products and categories drive the most revenue and profit?
- Who are our highest-value customers and how do they behave?
- How is sales performance trending MoM and YoY?
- Which regions are underperforming?

---

## Dashboard Pages

| Page | Content |
|---|---|
| Sales Overview | Revenue KPIs, monthly trend, regional breakdown, YoY & MoM growth |
| Customer Analysis | Segmentation, top 10 customers, new vs returning, purchase frequency |
| Product Performance | Top/bottom sellers, category contribution, profitability matrix |

---

## DAX Measures

```dax
Total Revenue    = SUM(Sales[Amount])
Total Orders     = COUNTROWS(Sales)
Avg Order Value  = DIVIDE([Total Revenue], [Total Orders])
Sales LY         = CALCULATE([Total Revenue], SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR(Date[Date]))
YoY Growth %     = DIVIDE([Total Revenue] - [Sales LY], [Sales LY])
Sales YTD        = TOTALYTD([Total Revenue], Date[Date])
% of Total Sales = DIVIDE([Total Revenue], CALCULATE([Total Revenue], ALL(Sales)))

MoM Growth % =
VAR Current  = [Total Revenue]
VAR Previous = CALCULATE([Total Revenue], PREVIOUSMONTH(Date[Date]))
RETURN DIVIDE(Current - Previous, Previous)
```

---

## Data Model

Star schema with one Fact table and four Dimension tables:
`Fact_Sales` → `Dim_Customer`, `Dim_Product`, `Dim_Date`, `Dim_Region`

---

## Tools Used

`Power BI Desktop` &nbsp;|&nbsp; `DAX` &nbsp;|&nbsp; `Power Query (M)` &nbsp;|&nbsp; `Star Schema Modelling`

---

## How to Run

1. Clone the repository
2. Open `Retail_Performance_Dashboard.pbix` in Power BI Desktop
3. Update the data source path via **Transform Data → Data Source Settings** if needed
4. Click **Refresh**

